>> title: Pan-Seared Pork Tenderloin with Caramelized Sage Apples
>> servings: 4

Preheat oven to 400°F.

Season @pork tenderloin{1.5%lbs} with @salt{pinch} and @black pepper{pinch} to taste, and half of the @fresh sage{1%tbsp}. 

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large #skillet over medium-high heat. Sear pork tenderloin on all sides until browned ~{2%minutes} per side). 

Transfer skillet to oven and roast for ~{15%minutes} until internal temperature reaches 145°F.

While pork roasts, melt @butter{2%tbsp} and remaining @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #pan over medium heat. Add sliced @apples{2} (Gala or Honeycrisp), remaining fresh sage, and @maple syrup{2%tbsp}. Sauté until apples are soft and caramelized ~{6%minutes}.

Remove pork from oven and let rest ~{5%minutes}. Slice thinly and top with the warm caramelized sage apples.